                  "title": "Compact syntax examples",
                  "content": {
                    "code": "x = 3  # comment does not execute\\nprint(x)\\n\\npath = r'c:\\\\new\\\\folder'\\n\\nnumbers = [\\n    1,\\n    2,\\n    3,\\n]",
                    "note": "Use brackets whenever possible; use an explicit backslash only when there is no bracketed structure to hold the continuation."
